  ├──────────────────┼────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │ round-trip       │ [38;5;153msetUser[39m then [38;5;153mgetUserId()[39m returns the id                            │
  ├──────────────────┼────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │ empty session    │ [38;5;153mgetUserId()[39m on fresh storage returns [38;5;153mnull[39m                          │
  ├──────────────────┼────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │ [38;5;153mclear()[39m          │ after clear, [38;5;153mgetUserId()[39m is [38;5;153mnull[39m and the key is gone               │
  ├──────────────────┼────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │ corrupt JSON     │ bad value in storage → [38;5;153mgetUserId()[39m is [38;5;153mnull[39m and the key is cleared  │
  ├──────────────────┼────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │ throwing storage │ [38;5;153msetUser[39m doesn't throw; [38;5;153mgetUserId()[39m still returns the id in-page    │
  ├──────────────────┼────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │ missing userId   │ [38;5;153msetUser({username})[39m with no id writes nothing; [38;5;153mgetUserId()[39m is [38;5;153mnull[39m │
  ├──────────────────┼────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │ one key          │ only [38;5;153m"app.session"[39m is ever written                                 │
  └──────────────────┴────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

  Written test-first, per the repo's TDD practice — each test fails before the behavior exists.

  [1mNot covered, stated plainly:[0m the form submit path, the [38;5;153mawait[39m in the handler, and the [38;5;153mindex.html[39m script ordering. Those
  need a browser or a DOM harness. If they matter to you, that's the e2e option you declined in Section 1, and I'd
  rather name the gap than imply the feature is fully covered.

  That's the last section. Next I write this up as a spec you can read in full, then you review it before any code gets
  written.
